.KEY prog/A,lang/A,quiet/S
.BRA {
.KET }
; gui-run - start one GUI program, check that it is still running after
; a few seconds, stop it with Ctrl-C and check that it is gone.
; Prints "ok ..." or "FAIL ..."; part of tests/amiga/gui-test.
; No $variables: not every shell expands them (ClaudeAmi's does not),
; backticks work everywhere.
;
;   Execute gui-run <program> <language> [QUIET]

Run >NIL: {prog} LANGUAGE={lang}
Wait 5
Status >NIL: COM={prog}
If WARN
  Echo "FAIL {prog} {lang}: not running after 5 s"
  Skip end
EndIf
Break `Status COM={prog}` C
Wait 3
Status >NIL: COM={prog}
If NOT WARN
  Echo "FAIL {prog} {lang}: still running 3 s after Ctrl-C"
  Break `Status COM={prog}` C
  Wait 3
  Skip end
EndIf
If NOT "{quiet}" EQ "QUIET"
  Echo "ok   {prog} {lang}"
EndIf
Lab end
